# The review machinery (ADR 0086): the files that decide how a pull request is judged and merged,
# and what agent sessions are told and allowed to do. A pull request that changes one of them, or
# renames a file out of one, is high risk: it merges only after the maintainer approves its head
# commit. Every other change gets the tier its blast-radius review judges, so this list names only
# what a session must not be able to loosen by declaring a low tier. Risk / risk gate reads this file from the default branch,
# so a pull request cannot change the paths that judge it.
#
# The patterns follow CODEOWNERS: a leading slash or a slash inside anchors a pattern at the root, a
# pattern with no slash matches at any depth, * stays within one folder, ** crosses folders, a
# pattern that names a folder covers everything below it, and one that ends in /* covers only the
# files directly in its folder. The gate refuses a pattern with whitespace, ! or [, so write an
# inline comment on a line of its own.

# CI, the gate and its scripts, and the meta tests that guard a control: a test of a file that
# GitHub, CI, Renovate, CodeRabbit or Claude Code reads, a test that is the only run of a rule the
# project relies on (a grant, a license boundary, a dependency rule, the hardening of the image and
# the Compose bundle), the test that every test file is collected, and the helper those tests
# share. The other meta tests check naming, layout and docs rules, and get the tier their
# blast-radius review judges (#977).
